        # [LOW] "silent as a shadow on stone" — voice signature comparison, acceptable.
        # [LOW] "the hush of the mesa to cloak your passage" — expands "silence" to active concealment metaphor; acceptable voice intensification.
        # [LOW] "the thread dyed to match the color of dust on the cliffs" — "dust on the cliffs" is INVENTION beyond "mesa dust."
        # [CRIT] "their edges faded by two weeks of sun and wind" — CONTRADICTION. The RECORD states the date stamp is "faded"; the transcriptions themselves are wrapped in oilcloth and have not been exposed to sun and wind.
        # [LOW] "the pigment bleeding at the corners where the ink clung too long" — LOADED EMBELLISHMENT. Adds a causal mechanism ("clung too long") not in RECORD, which only notes bleeding "at the edges."
